# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in as you connect each piece.
# The application runs with none of these set — it falls back to the demo dataset.

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When set, lib/data/index.ts should switch getRepository() from the demo
# repository to PostgresMarketDataRepository. See docs/DATA_PIPELINE.md §5.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/mtl_market
# PGSSL=require        # most hosted providers need this; local Postgres does not

# ── Supabase (alternative to a direct connection) ────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
#
# The service-role key bypasses row-level security. It belongs on the server
# only — never with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, which would ship it to the browser.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# ── Ingest authentication ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret protecting every endpoint under /api/internal/market-data.
# A scheduler (n8n, Vercel Cron, GitHub Actions, plain cron) sends it as:
#
#   Authorization: Bearer <secret>
#
# Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#
# Behaviour when this is NOT set:
#   - development / test : endpoints run unprotected and say so in the response
#   - production         : endpoints return 401 and refuse to run (fail closed)
#
# It is server-only. Do NOT rename it with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — that would
# inline the secret into the JavaScript every visitor downloads.
# MARKET_INGEST_SECRET=

# ── Pipeline alerting ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. When set, pipeline alerts are POSTed here as JSON in addition to
# being written to the server log. Any endpoint that accepts a JSON body works —
# an n8n webhook, a serverless function, your own collector. The payload is
# vendor-neutral; adapt it at the receiving end rather than in this codebase.
# PIPELINE_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
#
# Seconds an unresolved incident stays suppressed before it re-alerts. Keeps a
# pipeline that fails every 15 minutes from sending 96 identical notifications a
# day, without letting a genuine outage go quiet forever. Default: 21600 (6h).
# PIPELINE_ALERT_REPEAT_SECONDS=21600

# ── Upstream sources (added as connectors are written) ───────────────────────
# Most Canadian open data needs no key. A licensed listing feed will.
# LISTINGS_API_KEY=

# Mortgage rates. See docs/MORTGAGE_RATE_PIPELINE.md — the supported route is a
# licensed aggregator or manual entry, not collection from lender websites.
# RATE_FEED_API_KEY=
#
# The Bank of Canada Valet API needs no key at all, which is what makes it the
# right place to practise: https://www.bankofcanada.ca/valet/docs
#
# It is already integrated — connector, normalizer, validation, ingest service,
# repository and API. See docs/BANK_OF_CANADA.md. Ingestion needs DATABASE_URL:
# the demo fallback is read-only and refuses writes rather than accepting them
# into memory that vanishes on restart.
